rows.response:
The maximum administrative fines under the GDPR are as follows: 

1. Up to 20,000,000 EUR, or in the case of an undertaking, up to 4% of the total worldwide annual turnover of the preceding financial year, whichever is higher, for infringements related to:
   - Basic principles for processing, including conditions for consent (Articles 5, 6, 7, and 9);
   - Data subjects' rights (Articles 12 to 22);
   - Transfers of personal data to third countries or international organizations (Articles 44 to 49);
   - Obligations under Member State law adopted under Chapter IX;
   - Non-compliance with orders or limitations on processing by the supervisory authority (Article 58) [1].

2. Up to 10,000,000 EUR, or in the case of an undertaking, up to 2% of the total worldwide annual turnover of the preceding financial year, whichever is higher, for infringements related to:
   - Obligations of the controller and processor (Articles 8, 11, 25 to 39, and 42 and 43);
   - Obligations of the certification body (Articles 42 and 43);
   - Obligations of the monitoring body (Article 41(4)) [2][3].

