A DSA notice-and-action mechanism must allow users to submit notices that contain the following elements: 

(a) a sufficiently substantiated explanation of why the information is considered illegal content; 
(b) a clear indication of the exact electronic location of that information, such as the exact URL or URLs; 
(c) the name and email address of the individual or entity submitting the notice, except in specific cases involving certain offences; 
(d) a statement confirming the bona fide belief that the information and allegations are accurate and complete [4].

